WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.318
Parker Crane was born on May 19, 1920 in Hollister, California as the son of

00:00:04.324 --> 00:00:07.806
Michelle Crane and his father, whose name is unknown. The father was the one

00:00:07.828 --> 00:00:11.910
to bestow him with the name Parker, a boy's name, which his mother resented for some reason.

00:00:12.004 --> 00:00:15.518
If you can't tell, Michelle was completely psychotic and abusive as a mother, 

00:00:15.524 --> 00:00:18.366
and by the time that Parker was seven years old, the father was

00:00:18.388 --> 00:00:20.987
seemingly no longer in the picture, as far as we can tell. 

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:23.182
I'm guessing Michelle either took his life or her

00:00:23.236 --> 00:00:27.551
absolute lunacy scared him away, and leaving young Parker alone with his abuser. 

00:00:27.551 --> 00:00:30.742
The two moved to Los Angeles where Michelle decorated his room into

00:00:30.796 --> 00:00:35.229
a girl's room, complete with flowery wallpaper dolls and like seven wooden horses

00:00:35.229 --> 00:00:38.354
She also forced him to wear girls clothing and go around with a wig,

00:00:38.402 --> 00:00:40.322
insisting that he go by the name of Marilyn.

00:00:40.386 --> 00:00:43.834
On one occasion, when he drew his mom this picture and signed his name as

00:00:43.872 --> 00:00:47.354
Parker, she screamed at him and slapped the sh*t out of him before going on

00:00:47.392 --> 00:00:49.078
an unhinged tirade.

00:00:49.174 --> 00:00:53.310
- [MICHELLE] That is not your name, Parker.

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:55.598
- [MICHELLE] It's not your name.

00:00:55.764 --> 00:00:59.070
- [MICHELLE] That is the name your father gave you.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:03.498
- [MICHELLE] Your name is Marilyn.

00:01:03.674 --> 00:01:06.562
After threatening him into accepting this, she didn't stop there.

00:01:06.616 --> 00:01:09.970
She forced Parker to do horrible things to others for no apparent reason

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.794
other than having it out for the world.

00:01:11.912 --> 00:01:15.330
- [PARKER] If she needs you, she'll make me kill you.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:18.958
Whether Michelle lived on and continued to abuse him or not, the homicidal

00:01:18.974 --> 00:01:22.486
tendencies and cross dressing stayed with Parker into his elder years. 

00:01:22.508 --> 00:01:25.826
When he inherited the house and used it as a base of operations as he transformed

00:01:25.858 --> 00:01:27.726
into a full blown serial killer.

00:01:27.778 --> 00:01:30.951
To learn how Parker's childhood abuse carried over into the afterlife, 

00:01:30.951 --> 00:01:33.260
stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:33.260 --> 00:01:39.184
♪ Metal Music ♪

00:01:39.529 --> 00:01:40.746
Welcome to Horror History.

00:01:40.848 --> 00:01:44.154
The Bride in Black started as a minor character in the first Insidious, but

00:01:44.192 --> 00:01:47.326
people were so creeped out by him that he gained an expanded role in the

00:01:47.348 --> 00:01:50.042
franchise as the main rival of the hero, Elise Rainier. 

00:01:50.106 --> 00:01:52.602
The idea for the Bride to be a man was there from the beginning.

00:01:52.666 --> 00:01:55.866
He's played by Philip Friedman in the original, and then Tom Fitzpatrick

00:01:55.898 --> 00:01:58.210
takes over the role in Insidious Chapter Two and Three.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:01.730
The choice was explained by the creative team in the Blu-ray bonus features.

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:05.922
- [LEIGH WHANNELL] The old woman in the film is actually played by a man, which is something

00:02:05.976 --> 00:02:08.566
- [LEIGH WHANNELL] that James just thought would be a macabre touch.

00:02:08.668 --> 00:02:11.522
- [ELEANOR SABADUQUIA] When people asked him why, he said, It's just creepy.

00:02:11.586 --> 00:02:14.038
- [ELEANOR SABADUQUIA] It's just disturbing because there's something not right.

00:02:14.124 --> 00:02:17.606
So when Insidious chapter Two was conceptualized, director James Wan and

00:02:17.628 --> 00:02:20.646
screenwriter Leigh Whannell decided to expand the lore of this character who

00:02:20.668 --> 00:02:21.614
chilled audiences.

00:02:21.682 --> 00:02:24.794
But to understand what made the Bride and Black stick with audiences even

00:02:24.832 --> 00:02:29.210
after watching the film, we've got to take it back to his criminal career as a kidnapper.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:29.710
(IMPACT)

00:02:29.794 --> 00:02:33.901
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:02:33.901 --> 00:02:37.374
It's likely that Parker kept a relatively low profile throughout most of his

00:02:37.412 --> 00:02:37.982
adult years.

00:02:38.036 --> 00:02:40.906
Because the articles about the Bride and black all seem to refer to Parker

00:02:40.938 --> 00:02:41.722
as an old woman.

00:02:41.786 --> 00:02:45.106
It would appear that he is older when his mother started forcing him to kill. 

00:02:45.106 --> 00:02:47.906
I should note that it's not clear if Michelle herself was now an old

00:02:47.928 --> 00:02:51.566
woman manipulating him into doing these things, or if she died and her ghost

00:02:51.598 --> 00:02:53.170
was the one forcing Parker's hand.

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:56.066
It seems like when a person dies, their spirit resembles what they looked

00:02:56.088 --> 00:02:56.734
like at death.

00:02:56.782 --> 00:02:59.998
Michelle appears to be in her mid 30s as a ghost, so I think she died when

00:03:00.024 --> 00:03:02.774
Parker was young and continued to haunt him from the other side.

00:03:02.892 --> 00:03:06.118
However, there's no linear time in the Further, and those who enter the

00:03:06.124 --> 00:03:09.570
Further can see various incarnations of people who have not yet died.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:13.306
For example, Josh talked to a younger version of himself at one point, but

00:03:13.328 --> 00:03:16.474
it's not really important if Michelle was dead or alive when Parker started

00:03:16.512 --> 00:03:17.542
committing his crimes.

00:03:17.606 --> 00:03:21.326
As his nickname implies, Parker would dress up in a black wedding dress and veil, 

00:03:21.326 --> 00:03:24.698
put on makeup like an old woman, and kidnap exclusively females, which

00:03:24.704 --> 00:03:27.598
was probably to satisfy his mother, who had always wanted a girl.

00:03:27.684 --> 00:03:30.826
After capturing them, he would tie them up and choose from an array of tools

00:03:30.858 --> 00:03:32.478
which were used to finish the women off.

00:03:32.564 --> 00:03:35.738
Each of them was stored in the house in a secret room behind a bookcase.

00:03:35.834 --> 00:03:39.006
The newspapers would eventually report that he had 15 victims, but it's

00:03:39.038 --> 00:03:41.666
possible that there were more that the media just doesn't know about because

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:43.890
he always kidnapped his victims before killing them.

00:03:43.960 --> 00:03:47.342
Some of his victims seem to be located in and around Newark, California,

00:03:47.406 --> 00:03:50.978
which is in the Bay Area, only 65 miles from his birthplace of Hollister.

00:03:51.074 --> 00:03:53.878
However, Parker still lives in his childhood home in LA.

00:03:53.964 --> 00:03:56.646
He clipped newspaper articles about each of the women that he attempted to

00:03:56.668 --> 00:04:00.551
abduct, including one girl who got away and described her attacker to police. 

00:04:00.551 --> 00:04:03.334
Maybe Parker was able to get such a high kill count because nobody

00:04:03.382 --> 00:04:07.018
suspects an old woman of being a serial kidnapper unless given a reason.

00:04:07.104 --> 00:04:10.406
Eventually, simply dressing in women's clothing was not enough to satisfy

00:04:10.438 --> 00:04:13.354
his mother, and she forced Parker to attempt to castrate himself, which

00:04:13.392 --> 00:04:14.490
landed him in the hospital.

00:04:14.570 --> 00:04:20.159
He was admitted to Our Lady of the Angels hospital on September 20, 1986 at 3:05AM. 

00:04:20.159 --> 00:04:23.466
There he was diagnosed with paranoid schizophrenia and self mutilation.

00:04:23.578 --> 00:04:27.246
One day, as he was being tended to by medical staff, Josh Lambert, the son

00:04:27.268 --> 00:04:30.478
of one of the nurses, wandered into his room and seeing the boy, sent Parker

00:04:30.494 --> 00:04:31.502
into a fit of rage.

00:04:31.566 --> 00:04:34.014
He attacked Josh because he was so jealous of his youth.

00:04:34.062 --> 00:04:37.742
He wanted his childhood back, and this incident sent Parker over the edge, literally.

00:04:37.806 --> 00:04:42.300
Two days later, he jumped to his death, likely joining his mom in the Further. 

00:04:42.386 --> 00:04:45.506
His house is left abandoned and the bodies of the victims are not discovered

00:04:45.538 --> 00:04:46.406
for many years.

00:04:46.508 --> 00:04:50.034
A day after he passed away, he got into an elevator with Lorraine Lambert,

00:04:50.082 --> 00:04:53.398
Josh's mother, who doesn't realize that she's apologizing to a ghost.

00:04:53.494 --> 00:04:56.854
Personally, I think he was following her because he was not done inflicting

00:04:56.902 --> 00:04:59.018
terror on Josh or the Lambert family.

00:04:59.104 --> 00:05:02.618
Josh began experiencing awful night terrors and fits of fear, claiming that

00:05:02.624 --> 00:05:04.558
an old woman would come visit him at night.

00:05:04.644 --> 00:05:07.994
Lorraine dismissed his claims until she started to notice a mysterious

00:05:08.042 --> 00:05:10.378
figure in the background of Josh's photographs.

00:05:10.474 --> 00:05:13.834
At first, it appeared to be a camera malfunction, but over time it became

00:05:13.882 --> 00:05:17.530
clear that there was a dark Bridelike entity creeping closer and closer to Josh

00:05:17.540 --> 00:05:20.818
With each photograph that he appears in, eventually the Bride could be

00:05:20.824 --> 00:05:22.270
seen reaching out for Josh.

00:05:22.350 --> 00:05:24.654
This is because Josh is what's known as a traveler.

00:05:24.702 --> 00:05:28.114
He had the ability to astral project and when he did this, his body was left

00:05:28.152 --> 00:05:28.974
open as a vessel.

00:05:29.022 --> 00:05:32.502
But the process for a spirit to possess a living person's body takes time,

00:05:32.556 --> 00:05:35.254
which is required for the spirit to essentially get in sync with a new vessel. 

00:05:35.292 --> 00:05:37.190
Parker wanted to feel life again.

00:05:37.260 --> 00:05:40.646
He would later describe life as his happy moment in the sun, as opposed to

00:05:40.668 --> 00:05:42.550
the cold, dark afterlife in the Further.

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:46.026
He also wanted to target Josh because taking over his body would allow him

00:05:46.048 --> 00:05:47.830
to experience a normal boyhood.

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.966
However, Lorraine becomes concerned by the photographs and hires psychic

00:05:50.998 --> 00:05:53.862
medium Elise Ranier to investigate the source of the haunting.

00:05:53.926 --> 00:05:57.406
As you can imagine, this deeply upset Parker, and he would try to ward off

00:05:57.428 --> 00:06:01.203
the woman who was trying to cut him off from his best chance at experiencing life again.

00:06:01.203 --> 00:06:04.938
And Josh guides Elise to the so called woman who had been visiting his so called dreams. 

00:06:04.938 --> 00:06:08.430
And Parker lashes out, leaving a pretty nasty slash on Elise's arm.

00:06:08.510 --> 00:06:11.982
- [ELISE] I saw it would hunt him and it's not a friend, it's a parasite.

00:06:12.046 --> 00:06:15.474
Because of that little altercation, Elise hypnotizes Josh to suppress his

00:06:15.512 --> 00:06:18.618
memories and make him forget his ability to astral project, seemingly forever. 

00:06:18.654 --> 00:06:22.386
But this action would not go without consequence as Parker turned

00:06:22.418 --> 00:06:25.782
all of his attention to getting revenge on the woman who took away his best

00:06:25.836 --> 00:06:27.240
shot at life.

