00:07:37.410 --> 00:07:39.962
The Bride in Black had his sights set on Elise.

00:07:40.026 --> 00:07:41.486
However, there was an issue.

00:07:41.588 --> 00:07:44.926
Although Elise has the ability to astral project, she knows the dangers of

00:07:44.948 --> 00:07:47.502
going into the Further, so she rarely ever uses it.

00:07:47.556 --> 00:07:50.882
Despite this, Parker stayed with Elise for 20 years, waiting for his moment

00:07:50.936 --> 00:07:51.922
to get revenge on her.

00:07:51.976 --> 00:07:55.598
In 2006, he would get his opportunity when Elise's husband, Jack, passed away. 

00:07:55.614 --> 00:07:58.658
The official ruling was that Jack had taken his own life.

00:07:58.744 --> 00:08:01.846
Elise states that Jack had suffered from depression before, but she never

00:08:01.868 --> 00:08:03.158
thought he would go this far.

00:08:03.244 --> 00:08:06.434
Could it be that Parker was the one to take Jack's life in order to lure

00:08:06.482 --> 00:08:08.182
Elise into the Further? I don't know.

00:08:08.236 --> 00:08:10.780
But I do know that's exactly what Elise does.

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:14.770
- [ELISE] So I tried to contact him. I just couldn't help it.

00:08:14.864 --> 00:08:17.626
- [ELISE] I visited the Dark looking for him.

00:08:17.808 --> 00:08:22.630
- [ELISE] Something I'd never done before, something we living people are not supposed to do. 

00:08:22.724 --> 00:08:25.880
- [ELISE] But someone followed me back. A woman. 

00:08:26.026 --> 00:08:28.218
- [ELISE] An entity driven by evil.

00:08:28.314 --> 00:08:31.022
As you can probably guess, this was no woman at all.

00:08:31.076 --> 00:08:32.426
It was Parker Crane.

00:08:32.538 --> 00:08:39.026
- [ELISE] Ever since then, whenever I used my ability, this woman, I could hear her in

00:08:39.048 --> 00:08:44.866
- [ELISE] my head, screaming over and over that she's going to kill me.

00:08:44.968 --> 00:08:52.950
- [ELISE] I think, no, I know if I continue with this work, she's going to kill me.

00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:54.530
And so Elise retired.

00:08:54.610 --> 00:08:57.670
But like Tom Brady, she couldn't stay away from her calling for long.

00:08:57.740 --> 00:09:01.782
It's about 2007 when Quinn Brenner shows up at Elise's door asking for help.

00:09:01.836 --> 00:09:04.566
I'm basing that on the fact that Insidious Chapter Three takes place a few

00:09:04.588 --> 00:09:08.030
years before the first film, and the fact that Quinn has a T-Mobile Sidekick Three. 

00:09:08.124 --> 00:09:11.006
Quinn was trying to connect with her mother when she was intercepted by a

00:09:11.028 --> 00:09:12.794
demon known as the Man Who Can't Breathe.

00:09:12.842 --> 00:09:16.110
So Elise gathers the courage to go into the Further to investigate.

00:09:18.211 --> 00:09:24.055
- [Elise screaming and sturggling]

00:09:25.810 --> 00:09:29.426
As Parker pins her to the armchair and strangles her, her airways start to

00:09:29.448 --> 00:09:32.706
close in the real world as well. She's only just able to break free and escape the Illusory Realm

00:09:32.728 --> 00:09:36.158
Once she snaps back to reality, she tells Quinn

00:09:36.174 --> 00:09:39.680
that her otherworldly stalker was waiting for her and that she wouldn't be able to help. 

00:09:39.788 --> 00:09:41.366
- [ELISE] That's her, she says.

00:09:41.468 --> 00:09:47.030
- [ELISE] One day eventually, I'm going to die by her hand, and I believe her.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:48.470
And the Bride is not wrong.

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:51.558
But Elise's time in the sun would not come to a close quite yet.

00:09:51.644 --> 00:09:54.746
After some encouragement from a colleague, elise goes back to The Further to

00:09:54.768 --> 00:09:57.446
try to rescue Quinn, who has now been possessed by The Man Who Can't Breathe. 

00:09:57.478 --> 00:10:00.646
After delving back into The Further and spotting a man resembling

00:10:00.678 --> 00:10:03.854
her late husband, the Bride in Black springs out of the dark to attack her,

00:10:03.892 --> 00:10:07.102
pinning her up against a wall where we hear him speak for the first time.

00:10:07.236 --> 00:10:08.830
- [Bride in Black] This is how you die.

00:10:09.170 --> 00:10:11.306
- [Elise] Not today. It isn't. 

00:10:11.306 --> 00:10:14.654
It's elise uses some kind of YouTube women's self defense technique to break

00:10:14.692 --> 00:10:16.602
free and throw the Bride out into the dark.

00:10:16.666 --> 00:10:19.698
They square up, and when Elise challenges him, he slinks back into the

00:10:19.704 --> 00:10:21.138
darkness, defeated for now.

00:10:21.224 --> 00:10:24.864
At some point after this, I believe the Bride unsuccessfully attacked Elise again, 

00:10:24.864 --> 00:10:27.858
because when we see her sightings book in 2010, there's a picture of

00:10:27.864 --> 00:10:30.662
the Bride, and it's after the page where she wrote Quinn Brenner's name,

00:10:30.716 --> 00:10:33.762
implying that this was another battle that she fought after saving Quinn.

00:10:33.826 --> 00:10:37.126
The Quinn Brenner case introduced Elise to Specs and Tucker, who she came

00:10:37.148 --> 00:10:39.462
out of retirement to go into the ghost hunting business with.

00:10:39.516 --> 00:10:42.082
So it makes sense that she would have another encounter with Parker.

00:10:42.146 --> 00:10:46.553
2010 is also the year that Elise and Parker would have their final confrontation. 

00:10:46.553 --> 00:10:48.614
It seems like Elise knows she's putting herself in danger

00:10:48.662 --> 00:10:51.466
every time she goes into The Further, so she decides to only use the

00:10:51.488 --> 00:10:54.246
abilities that she can access from the real world, making it nearly

00:10:54.278 --> 00:10:55.774
impossible for the Bride to harm her.

00:10:55.812 --> 00:10:58.986
But her work would lead both of them back to someone from their past,

00:10:59.018 --> 00:11:02.926
Josh Lambert, the very same boy that Parker had tried to possess in 1986.

00:11:03.028 --> 00:11:06.522
This time, Josh's son, Dalton, has been coaxed into the dark realm.

00:11:06.586 --> 00:11:09.694
You would think Parker would just go after him because possessing Dalton

00:11:09.742 --> 00:11:11.410
would allow him to have a childhood again.

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:13.874
I think the reason he doesn't attempt to do this is because there is

00:11:13.912 --> 00:11:17.394
another, more powerful entity known as the Redfaced Demon, who is much

00:11:17.432 --> 00:11:18.734
closer to possessing Dalton.

00:11:18.782 --> 00:11:20.934
So it would be futile for Parker to try to beat him.

00:11:20.972 --> 00:11:23.638
Instead, he just waits in the Further for the inevitable to happen.

00:11:23.724 --> 00:11:27.174
Josh Lambert regains his childhood memories and ventures into The Further to

00:11:27.212 --> 00:11:27.990
rescue his son.

00:11:28.060 --> 00:11:31.606
He's successful at retrieving Dalton, however, I guess astral projecting for

00:11:31.628 --> 00:11:35.626
a long period of time after 24 years without practice can be exhausting, and

00:11:35.648 --> 00:11:39.151
Josh has to stop and rest for a moment, as Dalton continues onto his body.

00:11:39.151 --> 00:11:41.570
The Bride waits in this strange area of The Further. 

00:11:41.622 --> 00:11:45.434
On Josh's side, it appears to be a window, but on Parker's side, it's like a bathroom.

00:11:45.434 --> 00:11:48.494
Parker holds up a candle to get Josh's attention, as he had many

00:11:48.532 --> 00:11:51.966
years ago, causing Josh to take notice and confront him telling him to stay

00:11:51.988 --> 00:11:53.006
away from his family.

00:11:53.108 --> 00:11:56.446
This, however, was only a distraction to keep Josh away from his body long

00:11:56.468 --> 00:11:59.730
enough for the evil spirit to go back to Josh's body and possess it,

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:03.058
trapping Josh's spirit inside of the Further, where he sees the illusion of

00:12:03.064 --> 00:12:05.454
the Bride and Black fade away into the darkness.

00:12:05.582 --> 00:12:08.926
After finally claiming a new vessel in the world of the living, parker tries

00:12:08.958 --> 00:12:12.354
to blend in by pretending to be normal, which may be enough to fool Josh's wife.

00:12:12.402 --> 00:12:15.926
But Elise can see things that she cannot and snaps a photo of him to

00:12:15.948 --> 00:12:18.852
see what really came back from the land of the dead. 

00:12:20.562 --> 00:12:24.234
Having been discovered, Parker/Josh loses it and chokes slams Elise into an armchair,

00:12:24.272 --> 00:12:25.622
 just as he had in the Further three years prior.

00:12:25.686 --> 00:12:29.110
But this time, she doesn't have the odd physics of an alternate world to rely on.

00:12:29.152 --> 00:12:32.986
It's a strong 32 year old man versus an old woman, and Parker keeps his promise. 

00:12:33.008 --> 00:12:35.266
This is how she dies.

00:12:35.398 --> 00:12:38.734
Josh's wife, Renai Lambert, soon finds the picture of the Bride and looks

00:12:38.772 --> 00:12:40.650
back at Josh as if he killed Elise.

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:42.462
However, there's no proof that he did.

00:12:42.516 --> 00:12:45.694
And there wouldn't be much point in Parker getting into a living body only

00:12:45.732 --> 00:12:49.138
to risk spending his new life in jail because he got caught killing someone.

00:12:49.224 --> 00:12:50.690
So he allows Renai to live.

00:12:50.760 --> 00:12:53.906
So Parker plays the part of Josh Lambert as the family relocates to

00:12:53.928 --> 00:12:56.110
Grandma's house while the police investigate theirs.

00:12:56.190 --> 00:12:59.438
They wouldn't find anything because apparently it was Parker's hands that

00:12:59.464 --> 00:13:01.010
killed Elise, not Josh's.

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:04.198
I'm not entirely sure how that works, to be honest, but that's what the

00:13:04.204 --> 00:13:05.282
movie seems to imply.

00:13:05.346 --> 00:13:08.946
Renai tells Parker/Josh that she's seen more Paranormal Activity and it's

00:13:08.978 --> 00:13:12.054
happening again, but he brushes it off and sells her the story that

00:13:12.092 --> 00:13:15.430
something evil followed him out of the Further to get Elise, but that it was over now. 

00:13:15.472 --> 00:13:18.858
Parker's new lease on life may get him out of the depressing realm that

00:13:18.864 --> 00:13:21.814
he'd been living in, but he's still not able to escape from his mother,

00:13:21.862 --> 00:13:25.118
whose ghost continues to haunt him, and, by extension, the Lambert family.

00:13:25.204 --> 00:13:28.686
However, Parker/Josh insists that there's nobody there and implies that even

00:13:28.708 --> 00:13:31.982
if there was, it would be best for the family's sanity to just ignore it.

00:13:32.036 --> 00:13:35.134
Late that evening, Parker Josh tries to tell Michelle that she has to go away, 

00:13:35.172 --> 00:13:38.378
which Dalton wakes up and overhears, leading him to suspect that

00:13:38.404 --> 00:13:39.774
there's something wrong with his daddy.

00:13:39.822 --> 00:13:43.138
The next day, that is confirmed when he offers to take the boys to school.

00:13:43.224 --> 00:13:44.706
- [Parker/Josh] I'm going to take the boys to school.

00:13:44.808 --> 00:13:45.538
- [Parker/Josh] You should rest.

00:13:45.624 --> 00:13:48.670
If you've seen the first Insidious, you know Josh never has time to take the

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:49.302
boys to school.

00:13:49.356 --> 00:13:50.758
He's always running late for work.

00:13:50.844 --> 00:13:54.326
That afternoon, he would come home to find his mother had already taken the

00:13:54.348 --> 00:13:56.360
first shot at his new family.

00:13:56.634 --> 00:13:59.453
(IMPACT)

00:14:01.517 --> 00:14:05.170
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:14:05.310 --> 00:14:08.618
Parker/Josh comes home that afternoon to find Renai passed out on the

00:14:08.624 --> 00:14:12.310
sitting room floor and probably realizes that his mother had something to do with it. 

00:14:12.352 --> 00:14:14.022
That is Parker's mother, Michelle.

00:14:14.086 --> 00:14:16.094
He creepily smells her hair while she's out.

00:14:16.132 --> 00:14:18.878
Just a sign that it had been so long since he'd been able to experience

00:14:18.964 --> 00:14:21.758
these simple pleasures that the living get to experience, like the scent of shampoo. 

00:14:21.764 --> 00:14:25.662
However, he quickly realizes that his supposedly healthy human body

00:14:25.716 --> 00:14:29.759
is dying when he removes a tooth and catches himself looking pretty rough in the mirror.

00:14:29.759 --> 00:14:31.759
He's not ready to give up his time in the sun so soon

00:14:31.933 --> 00:14:36.451
and Michelle explains his condition by saying that his dead soul is killing Josh's living skin,

00:14:36.451 --> 00:14:39.420
telling him that the only way to stop wasting away is to kill Renai. 

00:14:39.486 --> 00:14:42.502
It's hard to say if she's telling the truth, seeing as how Parker's mom

00:14:42.556 --> 00:14:44.658
always encouraged him to kill from the beginning.

00:14:44.754 --> 00:14:46.790
Maybe she's just making that up because she's crazy.

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:50.006
And the real reason Parker's soul is rotting Josh's body is because he

00:14:50.028 --> 00:14:51.126
possessed it too quickly.

00:14:51.228 --> 00:14:54.346
For example, when a RedFace tries to possess Dalton, it's a process that

00:14:54.368 --> 00:14:57.446
happens over the course of a few months, whereas the Bride in Black gains

00:14:57.478 --> 00:14:59.430
entry to Josh's body in a single evening.

00:14:59.510 --> 00:15:02.774
When Renai wakes up, she's worried about the baby, but Parker/Josh insists

00:15:02.822 --> 00:15:05.070
that everything is fine, and she's asleep in her room.

00:15:05.140 --> 00:15:08.330
However, Renai is not calming down because she's seeing ghosts everywhere,

00:15:08.410 --> 00:15:10.058
almost like they're already dead.

00:15:10.154 --> 00:15:11.246
- [Parker/Josh] No, it's not.

00:15:11.428 --> 00:15:14.493
- [Parker/Josh] This is nothing like being dead. I know. 

00:15:14.493 --> 00:15:17.694
But then he catches himself and adds that he's been to the Further,

00:15:17.742 --> 00:15:19.470
and he's seen where these things exist.

00:15:19.550 --> 00:15:21.490
That's why he knows what being dead is like.

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:23.602
Okay, Josh, we totally believe you.

00:15:23.656 --> 00:15:26.514
He claims that if she ignores the specters, they will go away, which is

00:15:26.552 --> 00:15:27.410
clearly not true.

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:31.889
But before Renai even has the energy to object, they hear the piano playing downstairs.

00:15:31.889 --> 00:15:34.626
Parker probably realizes that it's the real Josh who is trapped

00:15:34.658 --> 00:15:36.450
in the Further trying to get Renai's attention.

00:15:36.530 --> 00:15:39.926
However, he does not recognize the tune as the song that Renai wrote for her husband, 

00:15:39.948 --> 00:15:43.936
 which makes him look even more suss, and he tries to deflect her attention. 

00:15:43.936 --> 00:15:46.186
- [Parker/Josh] Well, it's not the song that we should be worried about.

00:15:46.368 --> 00:15:47.754
- [Parker/Josh] Somebody is in this house.

00:15:47.872 --> 00:15:50.762
Didn't you just tell her not to worry about that, like, two minutes ago?

00:15:50.816 --> 00:15:53.814
Renai ends up going back upstairs to deal with Dalton's night terror.

00:15:53.862 --> 00:15:57.162
So Parker/Josh stays back and tries to send a message to the real Josh,

00:15:57.226 --> 00:16:00.710
telling him that he won't be able to reach her and that the shadows are his home now. 

00:16:00.804 --> 00:16:02.830
I'm not sure what the baseball bat is for.

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:05.641
Can you even fight a displaced spirit with a baseball bat?

00:16:05.641 --> 00:16:08.050
 I guess Parker would probably know better than I would.

00:16:08.120 --> 00:16:10.829
His physical deterioration continues the next day. 

00:16:10.829 --> 00:16:13.538
He stays home, claiming he's not feeling well, but wakes up to

00:16:13.544 --> 00:16:15.394
see Renai and Lorraine leaving without him.

00:16:15.432 --> 00:16:17.790
And later finds a note claiming that they went shopping.

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:20.242
Just then, he gets a knock on his door from Carl.

00:16:20.306 --> 00:16:23.234
Carl was friends with Elise, and he actually helped her suppress Josh's

00:16:23.282 --> 00:16:24.790
memory back in 1986.

00:16:24.860 --> 00:16:27.654
So although he claims that he doesn't remember him, it's possible that

00:16:27.692 --> 00:16:31.190
Parker does remember and still has it out for Carl all these years later.

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:33.082
Or maybe he just knows what he's up to.

00:16:33.136 --> 00:16:36.266
Parker/Josh invites him in, and after going to the kitchen to get drinks,

00:16:36.288 --> 00:16:37.850
he returns with a knife behind his back.

00:16:37.920 --> 00:16:41.946
He's smiling, but his smile disappears when he realizes that Carl knows who

00:16:41.968 --> 00:16:42.970
he really is.

00:16:43.120 --> 00:16:47.402
- [CARL] What is Parker/Crane holding behind his back?

00:16:47.466 --> 00:16:48.746
He attacks. The knife is dropped in the scuffle.

00:16:48.778 --> 00:16:51.998
But before Carl can jab Josh's body with a sedative, he finds himself in a chokehold. 

00:16:52.004 --> 00:16:55.658
Specs and Tucker rush in to save Carl, but Parker easily knocks out Specs, 

00:16:55.674 --> 00:16:58.974
and then somehow, after taking a taser to the back from Tucker,

00:16:59.022 --> 00:17:02.066
still manages to jam the sedative needle into the big guy's leg.

00:17:02.168 --> 00:17:06.002
As usual in a James Wan movie, it takes effect almost immediately, and he

00:17:06.056 --> 00:17:07.710
collapses right onto Specs.

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:10.754
Michelle speaks to him again, once again claiming that he'll need to kill

00:17:10.792 --> 00:17:13.974
others if he wants to stay alive, but he clearly doesn't want to do that and

00:17:14.012 --> 00:17:15.718
screams at her to get out of his head.

00:17:15.804 --> 00:17:19.206
I almost think that he kind of wants to just take over Josh's life so he can

00:17:19.228 --> 00:17:23.051
finally live out the normal existence that he never got during his own lifetime. 

00:17:23.051 --> 00:17:25.994
But now that his secrets out, considering Carl knows who he really is

00:17:26.032 --> 00:17:30.302
and other people probably do as well, he panics and doesn't know how to proceed. 

00:17:30.302 --> 00:17:33.046
It would appear he has no other option but to give into Michelle's

00:17:33.078 --> 00:17:34.582
demands and kill his wife.

00:17:34.646 --> 00:17:37.342
I'd surmise that the only reason he doesn't kill one of the three

00:17:37.396 --> 00:17:40.718
unconscious victims in the house instead is because Michelle only wants him

00:17:40.724 --> 00:17:44.606
to take female victims, just like the 15 female casualties that he took as

00:17:44.628 --> 00:17:45.486
the Bride and Black.

00:17:45.588 --> 00:17:48.434
This could be considered additional proof that Michelle was lying about

00:17:48.472 --> 00:17:50.670
killing in order to stop his body from rotting.

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:54.706
So Parker/Josh is probably the one to text Lorraine using Specs's phone and

00:17:54.728 --> 00:17:57.890
tell the two women to come back to the house, where he waits to ambush them.

00:17:57.960 --> 00:18:01.206
Here's another question how did Parker Crane learn to use a cell phone when

00:18:01.228 --> 00:18:04.614
he originally died in 1986? I'd have to assume he just learned from

00:18:04.652 --> 00:18:07.078
observation while being a ghost in the human world.

00:18:07.164 --> 00:18:10.166
When Lorraine and Renai get back, Parker/Josh charges them, and they

00:18:10.188 --> 00:18:12.034
barricade themselves in the room with the piano.

00:18:12.082 --> 00:18:15.146
Josh's hand is caught in the door, causing him to yell out and claim that

00:18:15.168 --> 00:18:18.458
although it hurts, he's missed feeling real pain, but not as much as he

00:18:18.464 --> 00:18:20.154
misses inflicting it on others.

00:18:20.272 --> 00:18:24.570
Did the taser not count as real pain then? This is kind of a 180 for him.

00:18:24.640 --> 00:18:27.726
Just earlier that day, he was pleading not to have to kill, but now he

00:18:27.748 --> 00:18:29.790
claims that he misses inflicting pain on others.

00:18:29.860 --> 00:18:32.970
My take is that Parker has developed sort of an addiction for homicide.

00:18:33.050 --> 00:18:35.886
We've talked about this for other villains covered on Horror History who

00:18:35.908 --> 00:18:36.842
have a lot of victims.

00:18:36.906 --> 00:18:38.198
One example is Jigsaw.

00:18:38.234 --> 00:18:40.914
He starts off with the intention of punishing those who have wronged him,

00:18:40.952 --> 00:18:42.766
but later on he just can't stop killing.

00:18:42.798 --> 00:18:45.490
So he invents excuses to capture more and more people.

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:48.674
So I think feeling pain essentially triggered that part of him and made him

00:18:48.712 --> 00:18:50.710
remember the feeling that he gets from torturing women.

00:18:50.780 --> 00:18:52.630
This could also explain what happens next.

00:18:52.700 --> 00:18:55.926
After he forces his way into the piano room, Renai flees the kitchen and

00:18:55.948 --> 00:18:57.426
beats him down with a pot somehow.

00:18:57.458 --> 00:19:00.138
But then he ends up whipping a tea kettle in her direction, which knocks her

00:19:00.144 --> 00:19:00.742
to the floor.

00:19:00.806 --> 00:19:03.930
As she crawls away, he explains that he never wanted to kill her.

00:19:04.000 --> 00:19:07.180
- [Parker/Josh] She wanted me to kill you, but I said no.

00:19:07.710 --> 00:19:11.226
- [Parker/Josh] But now I know she was right.

00:19:11.328 --> 00:19:14.346
He feels that she deserves to die because she's ungrateful for not

00:19:14.368 --> 00:19:17.940
appreciating her life, which is a hell of a claim for someone who once killed himself. 

00:19:17.978 --> 00:19:20.638
But I guess hypocrisy is not this guy's biggest problem.

00:19:20.724 --> 00:19:24.174
The possessed husband would go in for the kill, but help would soon arrive

00:19:24.222 --> 00:19:26.610
from the most unexpected of places.

00:19:26.920 --> 00:19:29.539
(IMPACT)

00:19:31.842 --> 00:19:35.076
♪ Suspenseful Music ♪

00:19:35.590 --> 00:19:39.566
As the cold, rotting hands of Parker/Josh grip Renai's throat, she briefly

00:19:39.598 --> 00:19:42.886
sees the true appearance of the entity that is attacking her, the Bride in Black, 

00:19:42.908 --> 00:19:46.102
grinning and laughing as he squeezes the life out of her.

00:19:46.156 --> 00:19:49.334
That is, until he is knocked in the head with a baseball bat by none other

00:19:49.372 --> 00:19:50.562
than Dalton Lambert.

00:19:50.626 --> 00:19:54.035
The boy that the Bride had allowed to escape from the Further a few days earlier

00:19:54.035 --> 00:19:56.102
was now proving to be quite a problem for him.

00:19:56.156 --> 00:19:58.770
This gives the family time to retreat into the basement.

00:19:59.094 --> 00:20:01.317
- [Robert Graysmith] Not many people have basements in California.

00:20:01.317 --> 00:20:05.342
As Parker/Josh goes all Jack Torrance, trying to break into the basement and finish off the family.

00:20:05.396 --> 00:20:08.558
The real Josh is hard at work with Carl and Elise in the Further trying to

00:20:08.564 --> 00:20:09.278
do his part.

00:20:09.364 --> 00:20:11.886
Elise suggests that the Bride has a home in the Further where all of his

00:20:11.908 --> 00:20:15.038
memories live, and their best shot is to use those memories to lure him out

00:20:15.044 --> 00:20:15.790
of Josh's body.

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:18.654
They eventually find a dilapidated house where they witness the key memory

00:20:18.702 --> 00:20:20.910
that sent Parker down the path to becoming a monster.

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:24.850
However, this time Michelle turns and sees Elise and Carl.

00:20:26.001 --> 00:20:32.318
♪ Suspenseful Music ♪

00:20:32.318 --> 00:20:37.834
(GHOSTLY SCREAM)

00:20:37.834 --> 00:20:41.770
So it's up to Josh, real Josh, to dispel this evil woman from Parker's mind.

00:20:41.840 --> 00:20:44.918
He searches the room containing all of Parker's victims, but he's caught by

00:20:44.944 --> 00:20:47.342
surprise when he discovers Michelle hiding among them.

00:20:47.396 --> 00:20:49.710
She grabs him by the neck and slams him into the wall.

00:20:49.780 --> 00:20:51.630
Time is running out in the physical world.

00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:53.482
Parker/Josh breaks into the basement.

00:20:53.546 --> 00:20:56.986
Renai is able to stall just a bit by beating him down with a pipe, and Specs

00:20:57.018 --> 00:20:59.858
wakes up and also unsuccessfully tries to slow him down.

00:20:59.944 --> 00:21:03.246
Meanwhile, Elise finds the young version of Parker in the Further and asks

00:21:03.278 --> 00:21:06.258
him to open the door to his memories so that she can destroy the memories of Michelle, 

00:21:06.264 --> 00:21:08.258
 claiming that it'll set him free.

00:21:08.344 --> 00:21:11.250
It's fitting that all of this business with Josh and his family started

00:21:11.320 --> 00:21:14.626
because Parker just wanted to have himself a normal childhood, and it would

00:21:14.648 --> 00:21:17.620
be the child who granted access for Elise to do this.

00:21:22.993 --> 00:21:30.355
(SCREAMS)

00:21:31.470 --> 00:21:35.658
So exactly what happened here, it's actually left somewhat ambiguous.

00:21:35.754 --> 00:21:38.958
The first time I watched this movie, I didn't understand why destroying the

00:21:38.964 --> 00:21:41.518
ghost of Michelle would kick Parker out of Josh's body.

00:21:41.604 --> 00:21:45.134
How do you kill a ghost anyway? After thinking more about the ending,

00:21:45.172 --> 00:21:48.498
my interpretation is that this area of the Further beyond the red door in

00:21:48.504 --> 00:21:51.986
Lorraine's basement, purely contains Parker's memories, meaning that the

00:21:52.008 --> 00:21:55.362
incarnation of Michelle we see in there is just Parker's memory of her,

00:21:55.416 --> 00:21:58.066
different than the ghost of Michelle seen walking around the house.

00:21:58.168 --> 00:22:01.574
By destroying Parker's memory of his abusive mother, he no longer has any

00:22:01.612 --> 00:22:04.662
reason to exist as the Bride in Black, so he moves on.

00:22:04.716 --> 00:22:07.618
The trope for many ghost stories is that the ghosts stick around to haunt

00:22:07.634 --> 00:22:08.262
the real world

00:22:08.316 --> 00:22:09.990
because there's some unresolved issue.

00:22:10.060 --> 00:22:13.078
With Parker's scarring memories of his mom finally taken care of, he can

00:22:13.084 --> 00:22:16.358
finally move on to whatever lies beyond the Further, Elise even alludes

00:22:16.374 --> 00:22:19.098
to the idea that the Further is just somewhere you pass through on the way

00:22:19.104 --> 00:22:20.202
to a better place.

00:22:20.336 --> 00:22:25.440
- [ELISE] We all passed through this place eventually, hopefully on our way to someplace better.

00:22:26.370 --> 00:22:30.366
- [ELISE]  I've seen that better place, but I came back here because I heard you calling. 

00:22:30.388 --> 00:22:33.934
Although in Parker's case, he's probably headed to the bad place.

00:22:34.052 --> 00:22:38.066
So essentially, Elise has finally defeated her longtime rival, even if she

00:22:38.088 --> 00:22:39.442
lost her life in the process.

00:22:39.576 --> 00:22:42.894
The character of Parker Crane exists as a maxim about child abuse.

00:22:42.942 --> 00:22:46.418
In real life, child abuse is especially harmful because as a child, the

00:22:46.424 --> 00:22:48.062
brain is still developing and growing.

00:22:48.126 --> 00:22:50.706
In the same way that it's easier to learn a language that you were exposed

00:22:50.738 --> 00:22:51.510
to as a child.

00:22:51.580 --> 00:22:55.078
It's nearly impossible to erase the damage caused by maltreatment from a

00:22:55.084 --> 00:22:55.590
young age.

00:22:55.660 --> 00:22:59.394
This can affect behavior, emotional well being, interpersonal relationships,

00:22:59.442 --> 00:23:00.722
and cognitive functioning.

00:23:00.786 --> 00:23:03.994
Once the brain is shaped by childhood experiences, these experiences will

00:23:04.032 --> 00:23:06.182
continue to affect a person into their adulthood.

00:23:06.246 --> 00:23:09.654
In this case, Parker was forced by his mom to act like a female and harm others, 

00:23:09.702 --> 00:23:12.906
which gave way to his alter ego as the serial killer the Bride in Black.

00:23:12.928 --> 00:23:17.080
In our world, the effects of child abuse may end at the end of a person's life. 

00:23:17.136 --> 00:23:20.458
But in the world of Insidious, that continues onto the afterlife,

00:23:20.464 --> 00:23:22.246
where the Bride continued his disturbing patterns.

00:23:22.278 --> 00:23:25.678
Ultimately resulting in the loss of the franchise's greatest hero.

00:23:25.774 --> 00:23:28.546
If you want to learn more about the world of Insidious and the Further, I

00:23:28.568 --> 00:23:31.506
highly recommend checking out that video on the left, where I analyze the

00:23:31.528 --> 00:23:33.582
main antagonist, the Redface Demon.

00:23:33.646 --> 00:23:36.946
There is more Insidious and Conjuring content on the way, so remember to

00:23:36.968 --> 00:23:39.522
subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors every week.

00:23:39.576 --> 00:23:43.378
Ring the death bell for all notifications, and I'll see you in the next one,

00:23:43.464 --> 00:23:45.726
assuming we both survive.

